{
  "id": "13-answer-with-the-word",
  "title": "Answer With the Word",
  "tenet": "Meet temptation with truth and action",
  "durationMs": 75576,
  "audioAsset": "kingdom/13-answer-with-the-word.mp3",
  "transcriptAsset": "assets/kingdom/13-answer-with-the-word.json",
  "text": "What could you say when an old urge returns before you have time to think?\n\nA young man kept reaching for his phone late at night. He disliked what he watched, yet the familiar hour and place made the choice feel automatic. One morning he wrote down the pattern without disguising it: tired, alone, phone beside the bed. He chose a passage about honoring God with his body and read it aloud at breakfast. At midday he read it again. Before bed he left the phone outside his room, prayed, and opened his notebook. Some nights remained hard. The new response was becoming easier to choose.\n\nWhen Jesus was tempted, he answered with Scripture and refused the false invitation. The written word was joined to an actual choice. A passing thought is not a verdict on your character, and repeating a verse is not a spell. Name one recurring temptation privately. Write its trigger, a fitting passage, and one practical exit. Read the passage morning, midday, and evening; say it again when the trigger comes. Ask the Holy Spirit for the freedom to choose love. If the pattern involves dependence or harm, seek trusted and skilled help as well. Grace trains us through honest attention, repeated truth, and faithful action.",
